{"unit_slug":"monk_martial_arts","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","bonus_action_quota","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_bundle family for ClassFeatureMechanics","justification":"Martial Arts is not an activation — it is a passive, always-on set of three conditional benefits that apply whenever the monk meets an equipment precondition (unarmed or monk weapons only, no armor, no shield). The current surface only supports ClassFeatureActivationMechanics (family: 'activation'), which models a discrete use-count trigger with a single effect. A new 'passive_bundle' family is needed to carry an equipment precondition and a list of passive sub-effects that fire unconditionally while the condition holds.","evidence":"You gain the following benefits while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"equipment_precondition","justification":"The three Martial Arts benefits are gated on an equipment state: (a) unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons, (b) not wearing armor, (c) not wielding a Shield. No precondition atom exists in the current surface. A new atom is needed to model 'benefits are suppressed when this equipment gate is not met'.","evidence":"while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_unarmed_attack (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Bonus Unarmed Strike grants the specific right to make one Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action — not a free full-action choice. The existing grant_extra_action gives an unrestricted extra action, and there is no way to constrain it to a single attack type. A dedicated effect atom is needed: { kind: 'grant_unarmed_attack', cost: 'bonus_action' }. The per-turn cadence also has no reset analogue in RestResetCadence (closest wrong fit is short_or_long_rest).","evidence":"You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"alt_damage_die (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Martial Arts Die lets the monk substitute the weapon's normal damage die with a scaling die (1d6 → 1d8 → 1d10 → 1d12 by class level). This is a die-override/substitution on a weapon's own damage roll, not an additional damage effect. No existing atom in ClassFeatureEffect covers die substitution. The DiceAmount type supports threshold_tiers scaling, but there is no 'override weapon damage die' effect carrier. Proposed: { kind: 'alt_damage_die'; appliesTo: WeaponFilter; scaling: DiceAmount } where WeaponFilter distinguishes 'unarmed_strike' from 'monk_weapon'.","evidence":"You can roll 1d6 in place of the normal damage of your Unarmed Strike or Monk weapons. This die changes as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Features table."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"ability_mod_substitute (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Dexterous Attacks lets the monk use DEX instead of STR for attack rolls, damage rolls, and Grapple/Shove save DCs with Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. There is no ability-modifier substitution atom anywhere in the surface. The existing roll_modifier (DiceDelta) adds a fixed die delta to a roll — it cannot swap which ability modifier is applied. A new atom is needed: { kind: 'ability_mod_substitute'; swapFrom: Ability; swapTo: Ability; on: RollKind[]; weaponFilter: WeaponFilter }.","evidence":"You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. In addition, when you use the Grapple or Shove option of your Unarmed Strike, you can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier to determine the save DC."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RestResetCadence.per_turn (or 'unlimited')","justification":"Bonus Unarmed Strike has no per-rest limit — the monk can use it every turn as long as the equipment precondition is met. The current RestResetCadence variants (short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long) all describe rest-based refills of a depleting pool. Bonus Unarmed Strike is not a pool at all. A new variant — { kind: 'per_turn' } or simply removing the resource/resetCadence requirement from certain activation shapes — is needed.","evidence":"You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. [No restriction on number of uses per rest.]"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.724}
