{"unit_slug":"halfling_luck","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"SpeciesTraitRecord (new UnitRecord variant)","justification":"UnitRecord = SpellRecord | ClassFeatureRecord | MasteryRecord. No SpeciesTraitRecord exists. The tracer's traceUnit switch covers only 'spell', 'class_feature', and 'mastery'; 'species_trait' falls through to the exhaustive-never branch and throws at runtime. A new top-level record variant is required before any species-trait mechanic can be traced.","evidence":"Tracer output: 'unhandled unit kind: [object Object]' (src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"reactive_trigger mechanics family","justification":"Halfling Luck is a passive always-on species trait. It has no activation cost, no use count, no rest reset, and no player-initiated trigger. The mechanic fires automatically when a specific die condition is met. SpellMechanics (activation, ongoing_effect, triggered_reaction, anchored_trigger) and ClassFeatureMechanics (activation only) are all player-driven. MasteryMechanics (on_hit_trigger) is weapon-hit-only. A new 'reactive_trigger' family is needed: a passive observer that opens a window on a die result condition and grants an effect.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, you can reroll the die, and you must use the new roll."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"post_roll_window","justification":"The trigger fires immediately after a d20 result is produced but before it is committed to resolution. No existing window atom covers this: reaction_window (caster's reaction to an external event), on_hit_window/on_miss_window (post-attack-resolution), post_action_window (after a creature acts on an anchor), turn_start_window/turn_end_window (turn boundaries). A new 'post_roll_window' atom is required to represent 'immediately after a die is rolled, before the result is used'.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test, you can reroll the die"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"die_result_condition","justification":"The trigger predicate matches a specific face (natural 1) on a specific roll scope (any D20 Test). No existing trigger or filter atom expresses 'the die shows value N'. AnchoredFilter covers creature exemption lists; ReactionTrigger covers attack-hit and named-spell targeting. A new 'die_result_condition' atom is needed with at minimum: the die scope (d20_test), the matched result (1), and optionally the roll kind.","evidence":"When you roll a 1 on the d20 of a D20 Test"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_roll_reroll","justification":"The effect is a mandatory reroll: the current die result is discarded and a fresh d20 is rolled; the new result must be used. This is distinct from (a) modify_roll_numeric (adds a fixed delta to the existing result), (b) modify_roll_advantage (grants an extra die and uses the higher/lower), and (c) any existing effect. The reroll is unconditional in direction — it does not keep the better roll — making it a distinct semantic from advantage or numeric bonus.","evidence":"you can reroll the die, and you must use the new roll"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RollKind: 'ability_check'","justification":"D20 Tests (SRD 5.2.1) encompass attack rolls, saving throws, AND ability checks. The current RollKind = 'attack_roll' | 'saving_throw' omits ability checks. Halfling Luck applies to all three, so 'ability_check' must be added to RollKind to correctly describe the trigger scope. Without it, any encoding of Luck's scope using RollKind would be incomplete.","evidence":"D20 Test — SRD 5.2.1 defines D20 Tests as attack rolls, saving throws, and ability checks."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90\n      throw new Error(`unhandled unit kind: ${String(_exhaustive)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled unit kind: [object Object]\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:90:13)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/4106011-halfling_luck/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.599}
