_override atom exists.","evidence":"When you use your Unarmed Strike to deal damage with that new growth, it deals 1d6 damage of the type in parentheses instead of dealing the normal damage for your Unarmed Strike, and you use your spellcasting ability modifier for the attack and damage rolls rather than using Strength."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"physical_appearance_change","justification":"Change Appearance grants the capability to alter physical appearance (height, weight, facial features, voice, hair, coloration, apparent species within same size/shape). It is a named mechanical capability reachable via the in-duration swap. While its consequences are partly adjudicated, the capability grant itself needs an atom so the graph has somewhere to point.","evidence":"You alter your appearance. You decide what you look like, including your height, weight, facial features, sound of your voice, hair length, coloration, and other distinguishing characteristics. You can make yourself appear as a member of another species, though none of your statistics change."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"InDurationSwapCost on selectable_form","justification":"The ability to swap between form options mid-duration at the cost of a Magic action has no structural home. StandardActionKind already includes 'magic', but there is no InDurationActionCost concept or mid-effect swap structure in the surface. The selectable_form operation needs a switchCost field of this kind.","evidence":"...during which you can take a Magic action to replace the option you chose with a different one."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'spell_root' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'activate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'spell_slot' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentration_lock' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentrate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'expi