scale_target_count node for this because the condition checks for 'choose_up_to + linear' regardless of whether perSlotAboveBase is zero.","evidence":"The maximum number of objects is equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; for this number, a Medium or smaller target counts as one object, a Large target counts as two, and a Huge target counts as three."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"per_size_damage_track","justification":"Animate Objects' Slam attack deals damage that varies by target size (bludgeoning for Medium/smaller, piercing for Large, slashing for Huge) with different upcast scaling per size category (+1d4/+1d6/+1d12 respectively per slot above 5). The current DiceAmount type supports a single damage track and DamageEffect has a single damageType. There is no variant for size-partitioned damage. This widening is best expressed as a sub-structure inside the proposed summon_construct operation, but is documented separately because it requires extending the damage model independently.","evidence":"The creature's Slam damage increases by 1d4 (Medium or smaller), 1d6 (Large), or 1d12 (Huge) for each spell slot level above 5."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"command_window","justification":"While the spell is active, the caster can spend a Bonus Action each round to mentally command any or all summoned creatures within 500 feet simultaneously, issuing the same command to multiple at once. This is a recurring optional bonus-action window on the ongoing effect that re-opens each turn. It is distinct from a one-time bonus action (like mark_transfer): it persists for the spell duration, not triggered by a single event. No existing atom — window or operation — captures a recurring per-turn optional command dispatch linked to summoned creatures.","evidence":"Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at 