le.","evidence":"\"be transported to a harmless demiplane for the duration\""},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"conditional_on_duration_expiry","justification":"If the spell lasts its full 1-minute duration AND the target is a planar creature type (Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey, Fiend), the banishment becomes permanent — the creature is sent to a random location on its home plane and never returns. This is an end-of-concentration conditional: 'if concentration held to natural expiry AND condition predicate on target type, then apply permanent effect'. The surface has no lifecycle atom or relation for this pattern. The `expire` atom marks when concentration ends but has no hook for conditional effects at that moment.","evidence":"\"If the target is an Aberration, a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend, the target doesn't return if the spell lasts for 1 minute.\""}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.345}
